From a857c3b9f02916b633fb0b6f676d14bbe9c0f090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:29:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/20] tu: Add VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric for A8XX

Read per-vertex inputs and barycentric weights natively from the varying
storage:
 - The hardware stores interpolation planes (v0, v1-v0, v2-v0).
 - bary.f at the constant coordinates (0,0), (1,0) and (0,1) returns the
   three vertex values.
 - Values are split into 16-bit halves so that the plane arithmetic stays
   bit exact.

Vertex order:
 - The hardware vertex order rotates with the provoking vertex and with
   screen position. A runtime discriminator, a flat id compared with a
   smooth id from the producer, recovers the Vulkan order, and a
   provoking_last driver parameter selects the mode.
 - Point and line topologies are handled through a shader key.

Producers:
 - The producer (VS, TES, GS or the native mesh stub VS) is rewritten to
   emit the extra outputs the fragment shader requests.
 - With pipeline libraries, the fragment shader records its request, and
   the producer variant is rebuilt at link time from retained NIR.

Behind TU_EXPERIMENTAL=barycentric.

VK-CTS on Adreno 840 (KGSL),
TU_EXPERIMENTAL=barycentric,mesh_shader,mesh_native:
  dEQP-VK.fragment_shading_barycentric.*      16563 pass, 0 fail, 4428 not supported
  (monolithic, pipeline_library and fast_linked_library: 5521 / 0 / 1476 each)
Not supported cases are double types (no shaderFloat64).
